# xk8 / xk9 : optimised connected-set enumerators — validation and k=12 re-run
# container: crdnotebook-2117576787076075521-ac5su0sz0r-69729, 15-core cgroup quota
# local: macOS, 10 cores, Apple clang

## what changed vs xk7
xk8: T(v) as a bitset over the 367 blockers; candidate adjacency as a bitset; only
     "active" candidates (those sharing a blocker with the current set) are scanned.
xk9: additionally maintains touchCnt[v] = |T(v) ∩ U| and popU = |U|, so the touch test
     and the union-size bound are O(1) instead of O(words).

## self-test (identical totals to xk7 => same enumeration)
xk8 --selftest 300  7 6 3   -> mismatches=0 positive=186  total=1125  max=44
xk8 --selftest 2000 8 7 6   -> mismatches=0 positive=1122 total=12824 max=245
