## k=12 re-run with xk9 (container, 15 threads)
K=12 n=367 m=16440 threads=15 connected=1 fast=1
ADJ built in 0.4 s
CONNECTED_SETS size=13 union<=12 count=0 seconds=22475.0
EXIT=0 ELAPSED=22475s

==> 22475 s vs 21724 s for xk7: NO speed-up at k=12 (3% slower).
    Reason: at depth almost every candidate is "active" (shares a blocker with U), so the
    frontier trick degenerates and the cost per node is dominated by the |A| conflict
    checks. The optimisation pays off only for k <= 9.
    The k=12 result is nevertheless an independent re-derivation (different data
    structures, same canonical order): count=0 confirmed twice.
